SUMMARY:Among the Wildflowers at Jack London State Historic Park
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a wildflower filled adventure through the park’s backcountry! This scenic outing features a 12-mile round trip hike through lush spring landscapes\, where vibrant wildflowers blanket the trails beneath towering evergreens. Along the way\, we will pause to take in the sweeping views of Sonoma Valley and appreciate the beauty of the season in full bloom. \nThis hike is considered moderate in trail steepness\, but it is a fairly long day hike\, so come prepared for a full and rewarding day outdoors. Be sure to bring plenty of water to stay hydrated\, a packed lunch to enjoy at our turnaround point\, and sturdy hiking shoes suitable for varied terrain. Trekking poles are highly recommended for added stability and comfort over the distance. \nMost importantly\, bring your enthusiasm for spring and a sense of adventure. \n 
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/among-the-wildflowers-at-jack-london-state-historic-park/
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park\, 2400 London Ranch Rd.\, Glen Ellen\, CA
CATEGORIES:Recreation
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://golocal.coop/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Wildflower-bird-hike-Jack-London-Park-s.jpg
GEO:38.35681;-122.54092
